{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.QBeta.YekutieliTrefoilDiscretization","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.QBeta.YekutieliTrefoilDiscretization","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":11,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.YekutieliTrefoilDiscretization.surface2Form_trefoil_dressing_invariant","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.YekutieliTrefoilDiscretization.surface2Form_trefoil_dressing_invariant","kind":"theorem","line":122,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/YekutieliTrefoilDiscretization.lean#L122-L132","doc":"**The dressing is irrelevant (sorry-free).** Shifting each handle holonomy by a central\nelement (the color/flavor scalar dressing) leaves the trefoil surface term unchanged. So the\nwhole `bring_color_weighted` `−h(½−δ/4)·1` interface dressing **does not contribute** to the\ntransverse curvature — only the BARE non-abelian crossing commutator `⁅A_a, A_b⁆` does. This\nprunes the interface search: the missing deuteron datum is a genuinely non-commuting pair of\ncrossings, not a scalar color weight. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.YekutieliTrefoilDiscretization.surface2Form_trefoil_eq_zero_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.YekutieliTrefoilDiscretization.surface2Form_trefoil_eq_zero_iff","kind":"theorem","line":111,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/YekutieliTrefoilDiscretization.lean#L111-L120","doc":"**Vanishing criterion / the transverse bridge (sorry-free).** The trefoil surface term\nvanishes iff the two handle holonomies commute. This is the missing bridge of `qou-prjo`: in the\n**abelian** `H₂(q)` strand algebra (single generator `σ₁`, `TrefoilSurfaceStateSum.commutator_zero`)\nthe handles commute and the term is forced to `0` — the `σ₁³` path gives nothing. A nonzero\ntransverse datum therefore requires the **non-commutative germ `Ring R`** level (where `F_q ≠ 0`,\n`germ-commutator-q-curvature.curvature_antisymm`), exactly as the qou-tw5z τ-shadow lesson\ndemands: the surface is the ONLY source, and only off the abelian shadow. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.YekutieliTrefoilDiscretization.surface2Form_trefoil_eq_germ_curvature","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.YekutieliTrefoilDiscretization.surface2Form_trefoil_eq_germ_curvature","kind":"theorem","line":99,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/YekutieliTrefoilDiscretization.lean#L99-L109","doc":"**Grounding in the corpus `F_q` (sorry-free).** The discretized trefoil surface 2-form\nequals the germ q-curvature of the two handle increments, in the exact form of\n`germ-commutator-q-curvature.lean`'s `Fq = (1+δq₁)(1+δq₂) − (1+δq₂)(1+δq₁)` (whose\n`commutator_eq_curvature` proves it `= ⁅δq₁,δq₂⁆`). So the canonical discretization of\n`½P∮∮[F_q,F_q]` over the genus-1 trefoil Seifert surface **is a single corpus germ q-curvature**\n`F_q(A_a, A_b)` — the \"data the corpus lacks\" (bean `qou-prjo`) grounded in the corpus's own\n`F_q`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.YekutieliTrefoilDiscretization.surface2Form_trefoil","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.YekutieliTrefoilDiscretization.surface2Form_trefoil","kind":"theorem","line":90,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/YekutieliTrefoilDiscretization.lean#L90-L97","doc":"**Trefoil specialization (sorry-free).** For the trefoil Seifert form the discretized\nsurface 2-form is exactly the commutator of the two handle holonomies (`V_{01} − V_{10} = 1`):\n`surface2Form seifertTrefoil A = ⁅A_a, A_b⁆`. The transverse datum is the non-abelian\nintersection of the two Seifert handles. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.YekutieliTrefoilDiscretization.surface2Form_eq_skew","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.YekutieliTrefoilDiscretization.surface2Form_eq_skew","kind":"theorem","line":82,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/YekutieliTrefoilDiscretization.lean#L82-L88","doc":"**Skew-only structure (sorry-free).** On a genus-1 surface, only the skew (intersection)\npart of the Seifert form survives — the symmetric self-linking part cancels because Lie\nself-brackets vanish and the bracket is antisymmetric. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.YekutieliTrefoilDiscretization.surface2Form","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.YekutieliTrefoilDiscretization.surface2Form","kind":"def","line":77,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/YekutieliTrefoilDiscretization.lean#L77-L80","doc":"**The discretized Yekutieli surface 2-form** (doubled, integral) on a genus-1 Seifert\nsurface with Seifert form `V` and handle holonomies `A`: `∑_{i,j} V_{ij} · ⁅A_i, A_j⁆`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.YekutieliTrefoilDiscretization.seifertTrefoil","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.YekutieliTrefoilDiscretization.seifertTrefoil","kind":"def","line":70,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/YekutieliTrefoilDiscretization.lean#L70-L75","doc":"The right-handed trefoil Seifert matrix `[[-1, 1], [0, -1]]` (genus 1). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.YekutieliTrefoilDiscretization.bracket_add_central","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.YekutieliTrefoilDiscretization.bracket_add_central","kind":"theorem","line":61,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/YekutieliTrefoilDiscretization.lean#L61-L68","doc":"**Central (color-dressing) invariance (sorry-free).** Adding central elements `s, t` (they\ncommute with everything — e.g. the `bring_color_weighted` scalar dressing `−h(½−δ/4)·1`) to the\ntwo arguments leaves the bracket unchanged: `⁅a+s, b+t⁆ = ⁅a,b⁆`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.YekutieliTrefoilDiscretization.bracket_skew","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.YekutieliTrefoilDiscretization.bracket_skew","kind":"theorem","line":58,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/YekutieliTrefoilDiscretization.lean#L58-L59","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.YekutieliTrefoilDiscretization.bracket_self","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.YekutieliTrefoilDiscretization.bracket_self","kind":"theorem","line":56,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/YekutieliTrefoilDiscretization.lean#L56-L56","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.YekutieliTrefoilDiscretization.bracket","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.YekutieliTrefoilDiscretization.bracket","kind":"def","line":53,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/YekutieliTrefoilDiscretization.lean#L53-L54","doc":"Ring commutator (the Lie bracket on `R`). ","signatureChunk":0}]}